  "problem": "The function $g(x)$ is continuous over $x\\in [-3,4].$ Some values of $g(x)$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-4$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $-5$ | $-1$ |\n\nWhat is the smallest possible number of solutions to the equation $g(x)=1?$\n\nThe equation $g(x)=1$ has at least\n{{field-1}} solutions.",
